"Manage your Lists (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-collections)\nciteturn1001view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":12}); Total lines: 184\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Library Listening Lists\nL13: ## Manage your Lists\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 9, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Manage your Lists\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: manage-collections\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: You'll find two types of lists in the Audible experience — personal ones you can create in your own Library and public ones curated by your favorite authors, narrators, and Audible editors. You can save these public lists to your Library from both the desktop website and app to make them easier to access and enjoy.\nL29: If you're looking for more information about your Library, please visit 【1†Manage your Library】.\nL30: \nL31: Note: The mobile website doesn't currently support creating personal lists.\nL32: \nL33: In this article:\nL34: \nL35:   * 【2†How do I create a personal list?】\nL36:   * 【3†How do I add titles to a list?】\nL37:   * 【4†How do I remove a title from a list?】\nL38:   * 【5†How do I remove a list?】\nL39:   * 【6†How do I follow public Collections?】\nL40: ## How do I create a personal list?\nL41: \nL42: In the app\nL43: \nL44:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL45:   2. Go to your Library.\nL46:   3. Select Lists.\nL47:   4. Select New Lists.\nL48:   5. Give your list a name and description.\nL49:   6. Select Create.\nL50: \nL51: You can start adding titles from your Library right away.\nL52: \nL53: On the Audible website\nL54: \nL55:   1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL56:   2. Select Library in the site's navigation.\nL57:   3. Select Collections.\nL58:   4. Select New Collection.\nL59:   5. Give your collection a name and description.\nL60:   6. Select Create.\nL61: You can start adding titles from your Library right away.\nL62: ## How do I add titles to a list?\nL63: \nL64: In the app\nL65: \nL66:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL67:   2. Select Library.\nL68:   3. Find the title you want to add.\nL69:   4. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL70:   5. Select Add to list.\nL71:   6. Choose the list to which you want to add the title.\nL72: \nL73: On the Audible website\nL74: \nL75:   1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL76:   2. Select Library.\nL77:   3. Find the title you want to add.\nL78:   4. Select + Add to… under the title.\nL79:   5. Choose the collection you want to add the title to.\nL80: ## How do I remove a title from a list?\nL81: \nL82: In the app\nL83: \nL84:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL85:   2. Go to your Library.\nL86:   3. Select Lists.\nL87:   4. Find the list that has the title.\nL88:   5. Find the title on the list.\nL89:   6. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL90:   7. Select Remove from List.\nL91: \nL92: On desktop\nL93: \nL94:   1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL95:   2. Go to your Library.\nL96:   3. Select Collections.\nL97:   4. Find the list that has the title.\nL98:   5. Find the title on the list.\nL99:   6. Select Remove from collection.\nL100: ## How do I remove a list?\nL101: \nL102: In the app\nL103: \nL104:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL105:   2. Go to your Library.\nL106:   3. Select Lists.\nL107:   4. Find the list you want to remove.\nL108:   5. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL109:   6. Select Remove from Lists.\nL110: \nL111: On the Audible website\nL112: \nL113:   1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL114:   2. Select Library.\nL115:   3. Select Collections.\nL116:   4. Find the list you want to remove.\nL117:   5. Select Delete collection.\nL118:   6. Confirm deletion.\nL119: Note: Once deleted, lists cannot be restored, and the list will need to be created again and the titles added manually.\nL120: ## How do I follow public Collections?\nL121: \nL122: You can listen to curated content by authors, narrators, podcast hosts and Audible editors by following these steps.\nL123: \nL124:   1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL125:   2. Browse to find and select a 【7†public collection†www.audible.com】 that interest you.\nL126:   3. Select Save to Collections.\nL127:   4. The collection will appear in your Library under Lists.\nL128: \nL129: Note: You can unfollow a public collection at any time by selecting your Library, Lists, then select Delete collection.\nL130: Did this answer your question?\nL131: \nL132: 【8†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL133: \nL134: \nL135: \nL136: 【9†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL137: \nL138:  Back to top\nL139: \nL140: 【10†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL141: \nL142: 【11†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL143: ## Need more assistance?\nL144: \nL145: 【12†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL146: \nL147: \nL148: \nL149: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL150: \nL151: \nL152: \nL153: Worst\nL154: \nL155: 1\nL156: \nL157: 2\nL158: \nL159: 3\nL160: \nL161: 4\nL162: \nL163: 5\nL164: \nL165: 6\nL166: \nL167: 7\nL168: \nL169: Best\nL170: \nL171: \nL172: \nL173: Region\nL174: \nL175: United States\nL176: \nL177: Language\nL178: \nL179: English\nL180: \nL181: Loading\nL182: \nL183: Manage your Lists 【13†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHelp Center Desktop (https://help.audible.com/s/article/view-your-goodreads-want-to-read-list-in-audible)\nciteturn1001view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":16}); Redirected to URL: https://help.audible.com/s/article/view-your-goodreads-want-to-read-list-in-audible?language=en_US; Total lines: 7\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: CSS Error\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManage Family Library Sharing (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-family-library-sharing)\nciteturn1001view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":17}); Total lines: 152\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Amazon Ask A Question Kindle Library Listening\nL13: ## Manage Family Library Sharing\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Manage Family Library Sharing\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: manage-family-library-sharing\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Amazon Family is a feature that allows you to share Prime benefits and a Family Library with members of your household. Through this feature, you can share your purchased Audible titles with one adult and up to four children. You can learn more about 【1†Amazon Family on Amazon's site.†www.amazon.com】\nL29: \nL30: Important — Platform availability:\nL31:   * Fire Tablet, Kindle, or Echo device: You can set up a Child account within Amazon Family.\nL32:   * iPhone, Android, or the Audible website: 【2†Create a Kids Profile】 instead.\nL33: \nL34: Amazon Family allows you to share your purchased Audible titles between two adult household profiles. However, 【3†Audible Premium membership】 credits or titles in 【4†the included catalog】 cannot be shared.\nL35: \nL36: In this article:\nL37:   * 【5†How can I set up an Amazon Family?】\nL38:   * 【6†How can I share audiobooks in my Amazon Family?】\nL39:   * 【7†Where can I access Audible titles that have been shared with me via Family Library?】\nL40: ## How can I set up an Amazon Family?\nL41: \nL42: Add an Adult account:\nL43: \nL44:   1. Go to the Amazon Family page on Amazon.\nL45:   2. Select Add Adult.\nL46:   3. You can either send an email invitation or sign up together to verify your accounts.\nL47: \nL48: Note: If you're sending an email invitation, the other adult will have 14 days to accept the invite. You can manage your invitation from Manage Your Household on Amazon.\nL49: \nL50: Add a Child account:\nL51:   1. Go to the Amazon Family page on Amazon.\nL52:   2. Select Add a Child.\nL53:   3. Enter the child's name and birthday.\nL54:   4. Select Save.\nL55: \nL56: Notes:\nL57: \nL58:   * Audible does not support Teen accounts at this time.\nL59:   * Audible-owned titles can be shared with another adult and up to four children. See where shared titles are available below.\nL60: ## How can I share audiobooks in my Amazon Family?\nL61: \nL62: Share titles with an Adult account:\nL63: \nL64: First, you'll need to set up an Adult account, then select the content you wish to share.\nL65: \nL66:   1. Go to the Manage Your Content and Devices page on Amazon.\nL67:   2. Select the Content tab.\nL68:   3. Select Audiobooks.\nL69:   4. Select an audiobook you own that you'd like to share from your Library.\nL70:   5. Select Add to Library at the top.\nL71: Note: With Amazon Family, all household profiles can listen to the same title at the same time without altering the Audible experience.\nL72: \nL73: Share titles with a Child account:\nL74: \nL75: First, you'll need to set up a Child account, then select the content you wish to share. You can share titles with a Child account through the Manage Your Content and Devices page on the Parent Dashboard.\nL76:   1. Go to the Amazon Parent Dashboard.\nL77:   2. Select the Child account you would like to share with.\nL78:   3. Select Content from the left navigation.\nL79:   4. Select Amazon Content.\nL80:   5. Select the Audible tab.\nL81:   6. Toggle on all titles that you own and you'd like to share with that child.\nL82: \nL83: Note: Audible's Kids Profile feature allows kids to listen to titles you choose by creating a Kids Profile on your Audible app.\nL84: ## Where can I access Audible titles that have been shared with me via Family Library?\nL85: \nL86: Titles shared to an Adult account can be accessed on:\nL87: \nL88:   * Audible for iOS app.\nL89:   * Audible Cloud Player.\nL90:   * Echo devices.\nL91:   * Fire Tablet.\nL92:   * Kindle app.\nL93: \nL94: Titles shared to a Child account can be accessed on:\nL95: \nL96:   * Echo devices.\nL97:   * Fire Tablet.\nL98: \nL99: Did this answer your question?\nL100: \nL101: 【8†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL102: \nL103: \nL104: \nL105: 【9†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL106: \nL107:  Back to top\nL108: \nL109: 【10†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL110: 【11†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL111: ## Need more assistance?\nL112: \nL113: 【12†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL114: \nL115: \nL116: \nL117: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL118: \nL119: \nL120: \nL121: Worst\nL122: \nL123: 1\nL124: \nL125: 2\nL126: \nL127: 3\nL128: \nL129: 4\nL130: \nL131: 5\nL132: \nL133: 6\nL134: \nL135: 7\nL136: \nL137: Best\nL138: \nL139: \nL140: \nL141: Region\nL142: \nL143: United States\nL144: \nL145: Language\nL146: \nL147: English\nL148: \nL149: Loading\nL150: \nL151: Manage Family Library Sharing 【13†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHelp Center Desktop (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-reviews)\nciteturn1001view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":29}); Redirected to URL: https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-reviews?language=en_US; Total lines: 7\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: CSS Error\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\n"
